finding: Stage 1 needs corrections (reviewed 45ffccc1 against 49fc69a7): P2 — The universal warning has a native-device blind spot. requestGPU unwraps the supplied device and only intercepts creation on its per-World Proxy (src/engine/runtime/gpu.ts:1257,1290-1457). Independently built an app, then created a valid compute pipeline through rawDevice(world.gpu.device): zero pipeline warning; creation through world.gpu.device warned. A caller retaining AppConfig.device has the same bypass, so the browser fixture cannot fail on that class. Either close the promised class or explicitly resolve/narrow the universal contract; add a negative control. A second World sharing the device did warn correctly through its own proxy. P2 — Deferred pipeline ownership is lost across awaited lifecycle work. withPipelineOwner restores guard.plugin as soon as operation returns its Promise (gpu.ts:635-649); trackedShaderModule records only that synchronous guard (1321-1324). Reproduction: AsyncOwner.warm awaits Promise.resolve(), creates a shader module, then after createApp resolves a pipeline using that module is created via world.gpu.device. Its warning says owned by "unattributed", not AsyncOwner. The existing tests cover only synchronous warm ownership. Preserve ownership for supported async preparation/deferred creation or provide an explicit required attribution contract and test it. P2 — New preparation compiles unused variants. RenderingPlugin.warm unconditionally calls warmUpscaling, which forces a native upscaling pipeline even with no cameras or stacks (substrate.ts:599; upscaling.ts:58). Independently counted native creations for defaults:false/plugins:[RenderingPlugin], no cameras: ["upscaling"]. Text and lines likewise force both 1x/4x variants; both motes plugins explicitly force rgba16float 1x and SAMPLE_COUNT regardless of initial cameras. This does not meet the requested composition-only preparation and adds startup compilation to compositions that never draw those variants. Select required variants from the composition and cover absent/one-variant compositions with counts. Checks independently passed: six engine warning/hook tests; seven headless shared browser controls; 28 tests across the six runtime-warning migration files and CLI create; five headless minimal browser cases. Four direct native controls (compute/render, sync/async) each emitted exactly one correctly attributed warning. No pre-land sweep or headed browser run. Migration audit is partial beyond the six intentional-runtime files; no additional migration finding established.
